HIGHEST-PRIORITY PROJECT FAMILIES (data-supported, clinically important):

1. FIRST-LINE TREATMENT SELECTION & OUTCOMES IN THE ICI ERA
   Core question: How are patients selected for AB vs STRIDE vs other ICI at JHU?
   Cohort: 136 modern RC HC true-1L (58 AB, 37 STRIDE, 31 other)
   Unique: Largest single-center AB vs STRIDE descriptive comparison
   Endpoints: treatment selection predictors, OS, PFS, toxicity
   Power: DESCRIPTIVE yes, COMPARATIVE marginal

2. ATEZO/BEV COMPONENT MODIFICATION IN REAL WORLD
   Core question: When/why is bevacizumab discontinued while atezolizumab continues?
   Cohort: 144 AB patients; 22 permanent bev stop, 22 fewer bev
   Unique: Admin-level IV component resolution (REACH has MAR data)
   Endpoints: modification rate, timing, structured reasons, outcomes
   Power: DESCRIPTIVE excellent, OUTCOMES modest

3. DYNAMIC LIVER-RESERVE (ALBI) TRAJECTORY ON FIRST-LINE ICI
   Core question: How does ALBI change during 1L therapy, and does early change predict outcomes?
   Cohort: 532 with baseline ALBI, 493 with delta
   Unique: Large cohort with pre/on-treatment ALBI dynamics
   Endpoints: ALBI grade worsening, ALBI delta as prognostic biomarker
   Power: EXCELLENT

4. EARLY AFP DYNAMICS AS TREATMENT RESPONSE BIOMARKER
   Core question: Does early AFP change predict outcomes in HCC ICI era?
   Cohort: 237 with baseline AFP, 171 with week-6 AFP
   Unique: Real-world AFP dynamics across multiple regimens
   Endpoints: AFP response rate, AFP as outcome predictor
   Power: GOOD

5. TUMOR-BIOLOGY x LIVER-RESERVE INTERACTION
   Core question: Do AFP and ALBI dynamics jointly predict outcomes?
   Cohort: 103 with both AFP and ALBI dynamics
   Unique: Novel combined phenotype classification
   Endpoints: 4-quadrant state distribution, OS by combined state
   Power: MODEST but sufficient for descriptive

6. FIRST-LINE FAILURE MODES & POST-1L OUTCOMES
   Core question: What happens after 1L stops? Who gets 2L? Who goes to hospice?
   Cohort: 282 HC true-1L
   Unique: Granular failure mode classification
   Endpoints: failure mode distribution, 2L uptake, time-to-2L
   Power: EXCELLENT

7. POST-ICI SECOND-LINE TREATMENT PATTERNS
   Core question: What 2L is given after ICI 1L, and do patterns differ by 1L regimen?
   Cohort: 65 reaching 2L from ICI 1L (242 total ICI 1L)
   Unique: Real-world 2L after ICI with administration-level data
   Endpoints: 2L regimen distribution, 1L->2L transitions
   Power: DESCRIPTIVE yes, OUTCOMES limited

8. ICI-ASSOCIATED HEPATOTOXICITY AND RECHALLENGE
   Core question: How often does transaminitis occur? Who gets rechallenged with ICI?
   Cohort: 228 transaminitis-evaluable, 79 ICI rechallenged
   Unique: Structured liver injury + rechallenge patterns
   Endpoints: transaminitis rate by regimen, rechallenge outcomes
   Power: GOOD for descriptive, MODEST for rechallenge outcomes

9. INCIDENT DECOMPENSATION DURING SYSTEMIC THERAPY
   Core question: How often do patients develop NEW decomp on therapy?
   Cohort: 282 HC true-1L, ~75 incident decomp events
   Unique: Incident (not prevalent) decomp classification
   Endpoints: incident decomp rate by regimen, decomp type distribution
   Power: GOOD

10. TREATMENT ERA EVOLUTION AT A HIGH-VOLUME CENTER
    Core question: How have HCC treatment patterns changed 2015-2026?
    Cohort: 569 first-line patients spanning 6 eras
    Unique: 11-year longitudinal view with consistent data infrastructure
    Endpoints: regimen share by era, uptake curves
    Power: EXCELLENT

11. HCC HEALTH DISPARITIES: A PREDOMINANTLY HISPANIC COHORT
    Core question: How do treatment patterns/outcomes differ by race/ethnicity?
    Cohort: 571 systemic (83% Hispanic, unique nationally)
    Unique: EXTREMELY RARE large Hispanic-majority HCC cohort
    Endpoints: regimen selection by race, OS by race/ethnicity
    Power: EXCELLENT (for Hispanic group); minority groups small

12. CONVERSION SURGERY & LRT AFTER SYSTEMIC THERAPY
    Core question: Who undergoes surgery/LRT after systemic, and what are outcomes?
    Cohort: 73 conversion surgery, 154 LRT after systemic
    Unique: Large conversion surgery cohort from single center
    Endpoints: conversion rate, procedure types, post-procedure outcomes
    Power: EXCELLENT

