PART 26 — WHAT REACH IS UNIQUELY GOOD AT
================================================================================

REACH UNIQUE ADVANTAGES FOR HCC MED-ONC RESEARCH:

1. ADMINISTRATION-LEVEL IV DATA (MAR)
   - Actual dates of each atezolizumab, bevacizumab, nivolumab, etc. infusion
   - Enables component modification analysis (Bev hold/stop)
   - NOT available in claims data, tumor registries, or most EHR studies

2. PREDOMINANTLY HISPANIC COHORT (83%)
   - Nationally unique ethnic composition for HCC
   - Enables disparities research in an underrepresented population
   - Most published HCC series are <10% Hispanic

3. LONG LONGITUDINAL SPAN (2015-2026)
   - Pre-ICI, single-agent ICI, combo ICI eras all represented
   - 569 first-line patients spanning entire modern treatment evolution

4. GRANULAR TREATMENT LINE VALIDATION
   - True first-line classification with high-confidence flags
   - Research status (routine care vs. trial) per patient
   - Post-1L state classification (progression, hospice, censor, etc.)

5. RECONSTRUCTED LIVER RESERVE (ALBI + Child-Pugh)
   - 532 patients with dynamic ALBI (baseline + on-treatment)
   - Lab-level longitudinal data for ALBI trajectory analysis

6. RICH TUMOR BIOLOGY (AFP)
   - 2,495 patients with AFP measurements, 237 HC true-1L with baseline AFP
   - Week-6 and week-12 landmark AFP dynamics available

7. DECOMPENSATION PHENOTYPING
   - 26,207 validated events across 1,768 patients
   - Incident vs prevalent decomp classification possible
   - Ascites, paracentesis, encephalopathy, variceal bleed, SBP, hepatorenal

8. COMPLETE JOURNEY MAP
   - 11,843 journey events across 3,999 patients
   - TACE, ablation, resection, transplant, SBRT, Y90, systemic, death
   - Enables multimodal treatment sequencing analysis

9. BEACON INTEGRATION
   - Protocol-level treatment plan data for ICI regimens
   - Validates regimen classification and identifies research protocols

KEY LIMITATIONS:
  - ECOG performance status NOT reliably captured
  - Child-Pugh is RECONSTRUCTED, not clinician-documented
  - Oral TKI adherence/actual exposure UNCERTAIN (orders only, no MAR)
  - Imaging response (RECIST/mRECIST) NOT available in structured data
  - Single-center (generalizability vs. depth tradeoff)
  - Steroid exposure DATA GAP (0 orders found — likely data quality issue)

